---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";

/*
 * Prerendered long-form document page. Content takes the full container -
 * no width caps anywhere, long-form pages included. There is no character
 * cap on body copy on any page in this app.
 *
 * LAST_UPDATED is a hand-set constant, not `new Date()` - a prerendered
 * page only regenerates when someone runs a build, and a date that quietly
 * relabels itself on every unrelated rebuild would say "updated" about
 * content that did not change. Bump it only when this page's text changes.
 *
 * Plain-language policy for the product as it exists today. Not legal
 * advice.
 */
const LAST_UPDATED = "2026-08-31";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - Motificons"
  description="What Motificons collects, why, and what it does not - in plain language."
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main" class="pb-24">
    <div class="page-container">
      <h1 class="pt-10 text-h1 font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-meta text-ink-muted">Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

      <div class="mt-8 text-body text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          Motificons is a free, open-source icon library: browse, search and
          download without paying anything. This page explains what we
          collect to run that, plainly enough that you should not need a
          lawyer to read it. It is not legal advice - if you need that, ask
          a lawyer, not this page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">The short version</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 flex list-none flex-col gap-2 text-body text-ink-muted">
          <li>Browsing, searching and downloading icons needs no account and no email.</li>
          <li>We never sell your data, and there are no ad trackers on this site.</li>
          <li>An account exists only if you sign in - it stores your email, nothing else you did not put there.</li>
          <li>There is nothing to pay for, so we never ask for or handle payment details of any kind.</li>
          <li>Icons keep their own upstream licenses; this policy is about your data, not icon copyright - see <a href="/licenses" class="prose-link">/licenses</a> for that.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">What we collect</h2>

        <h3 class="mt-8 text-h3 font-semibold">Cookies</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          We and our service providers use cookies, which may be stored on
          your computer when you visit the site. Most browsers allow you to
          refuse and delete cookies. You can find more information about
          cookies at <a href="https://www.allaboutcookies.org" class="prose-link" rel="noopener" target="_blank">allaboutcookies.org</a>.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-8 text-h3 font-semibold">If you create an account</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          Signing in stores your email address, tied to your account, so you
          can get back in. We use magic links by default (a one-time sign-in
          link sent to your email, no password to leak) - if you use Google,
          GitHub or Apple sign-in instead, we receive whatever minimal
          profile information that provider shares to identify you, never
          your password there either. Your session is a cookie that proves
          you are signed in; we also keep the IP address and browser that
          created each session, standard practice for spotting account abuse,
          not for tracking you elsewhere.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          Whatever you build with an account - collection names, saved icons,
          style settings - is stored so it is there next time. It is yours;
          we do not look through it except to fix a bug you reported or
          respond to abuse.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-8 text-h3 font-semibold">API keys, for MCP and automation</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          An API key is shown to you exactly once, at creation. We store
          it only in a one-way encrypted form, never the key itself, so even
          we cannot recover a key you have lost; you can only revoke it and
          make a new one.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-8 text-h3 font-semibold">Payment</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          There is none. Motificons is free and open source, with nothing to
          buy, so there is no checkout, no billing record and no payment
          processor anywhere in this list.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">What we do not do</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 flex list-none flex-col gap-2 text-body text-ink-muted">
          <li>No third-party ad networks, no ad trackers, no cross-site tracking.</li>
          <li>We never sell, rent or trade your data to anyone, for any reason.</li>
          <li>We do not load fonts, scripts or assets from third-party CDNs at runtime - everything is self-hosted, so no third party sees your requests just from visiting the site.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Who else sees any of this</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          A short, complete list - not a chain of undisclosed sub-processors:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 flex list-none flex-col gap-2 text-body text-ink-muted">
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Cloudflare</strong> - hosts the entire site, the database and the search index. Nothing runs anywhere else.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Resend</strong> - delivers sign-in emails on our behalf. It sees the email address a link is sent to and nothing more.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">PostHog (EU)</strong> - our product analytics, hosted in the EU. It measures page views and clicks; if you are signed in, your account email is linked to that usage so we can understand and improve Motificons. We never sell this data.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Ahrefs</strong> - privacy-friendly, cookieless website analytics for aggregate traffic measurement.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Your rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          Wherever you are - this is written with EU/GDPR rights in mind
          because they are a good baseline for everyone, not because of
          where you live. You can ask us to:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 flex list-none flex-col gap-2 text-body text-ink-muted">
          <li><strong class="text-ink">See</strong> what we hold about your account.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Correct</strong> anything that is wrong.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Delete</strong> your account and everything tied to it - do it yourself any time from your dashboard, or email us and we'll do it by hand.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Export</strong> your collections in a plain format.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          Email <a href="mailto:hello@motificons.app" class="prose-link">hello@motificons.app</a> for any of the above.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Icons are not your data</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          Every icon in the library carries its own open-source license from
          its original author, unrelated to this privacy policy - it governs
          your data, not your right to use an icon. See <a href="/licenses" class="prose-link">/licenses</a> for exactly
          what each license asks of you, and every icon page states its own.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Children</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          Motificons is not directed at children and we do not knowingly
          collect data from anyone under 16. If you believe a child has
          created an account, email us and we will remove it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted">
          If this changes in any material way, the date at the top of this
          page changes with it. We will not quietly narrow your rights or
          widen what we collect without saying so here.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Card variant="standard" class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-h3 font-semibold">Questions</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-meta text-ink-muted">
          Email <a href="mailto:hello@motificons.app" class="prose-link">hello@motificons.app</a>
          - a person reads it, not a ticket queue.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
